## C. THE REAL BLOCKER: NEITHER LANE IS CONSULTED ANY MORE
--- plant: append a line of C that CANNOT compile, then emit and run
    to tinybendygrad/runtime/dtype.c:  THIS_IS_NOT_C_AND_MUST_NOT_COMPILE %%
--- $ ./bin/bend abi_probe.bend -o probe.gen.c   ->  WITHIN-LIMITS rc=0 (emits anyway)
--- $ cc -O1 -w -o probe.gen probe.gen.c && ./probe.gen
    12/12 rows, rc 0, IDENTICAL to the unplanted run.
--- $ node probe.js                                      ->  12/12 rows, rc 0.
--- same plant on dtype.js (THIS_IS_NOT_JS syntax ((( error):  bend rc 0, node rc 0, 12/12.

    grep -c THIS_IS_NOT_C <probe.gen.c>  = 0
    grep -c THIS_IS_NOT_JS <probe.js>    = 0
    grep -c i64_of        <probe.gen.c>  = 0   (dtype.c has 7)
    grep -c pack64        <probe.gen.c>  = 0   (dtype.c has 8)
    grep -c dtype.js      <probe.js>     = 0
    AT 135bf0204, .agents/slop/abi/gen/probe.gen.c had i64_of x7 and pack64 x8 -- dtype.c WAS inlined.

    $ git grep -c 'import "./runtime/dtype' -- 'tinybendygrad/*.bend'
      135bf0204: tinybendygrad/dtype.bend = 20
      HEAD:      0
    The seams are PURE Bend now, so the .bend no longer imports the lanes,
    the emitted probe no longer CONTAINS them, and patching dtype.c/dtype.js
    is patching a file nothing reads.  THAT is why all 10 plants moved 0/12.
